A||||3||GT Bastard||Heads are off... Question!!||||5||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||05-17-2000||03:30 PM||||Upon pulling the head, Immediately noticed that the top of each piston was black.  My first reaction was "oh f*ck, they're burnt!!!!!!!!!!!!!"  I called my dad, and he was like, "That's ok, unleaded gas leaves a black residue.  If they were burned, they would look really clean with strange discoloring."  I just expected them to look nice and shiney, but is he right?  Also the cylinder bores feel smooth as can be, with no ridges or abnormalities.  Supposedly, this is a re-built engine too.  The main problem was just leaky exhust manifolds and bad valve seals.  So am I ok?  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Alex4mula||05-17-2000||04:45 PM||||That was my reaction when I took my heads off too. Mine had about 80K miles. Top of all pistons had hard black carbon residue film. Nothing to worry unless you see a crack or other major thing. Before putting heads back I tried to clean/remove as much as I can. Used a plastic scraper, a rag with solvent and a vacuum cleaner to suck the small pieces. Didn't spent too much time because it was a temporary fix.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||05-17-2000||04:48 PM||||That's just typical carbon build-up that all engines get.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eric||05-17-2000||11:21 PM||||You can leave it on and get a higher compression ratio  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
